From 2da1d9d279ec9857335fed41dfce3e79d222fbd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim auf der Landwehr <tadl-git@taufderl.de>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:07:02 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/3] nfc: st21nfcd: add STMicroelectronics ST21NFCD driver

Add an I2C driver for the ST21NFCD NFC controller. Unlike the
ST21NFCB/C handled by st-nci, this part speaks plain NCI with no
link-layer framing, so the transport is a thin one: send an NCI
frame as an I2C write, and on an interrupt read the NCI header and
then its payload.

ST does not publish a datasheet for this part. Two values were
established by observation on a Fairphone 4 and are commented as
such: the 0x7e byte the controller returns on a read when it has
nothing to send, and the proprietary RF protocol number (0x90) it
reports for MIFARE Classic, which the NCI core would otherwise drop
as unmappable. Both are the kind of detail a datasheet would settle.

Tested on a Fairphone 4 (ST21NFCD on I2C): the controller completes
NCI 2.0 initialisation, RF discovery runs, and a MIFARE Classic 4K
card is detected with its SENS_RES/SEL_RES and UID reported to
userspace.

Signed-off-by: Tim auf der Landwehr <tadl-git@taufderl.de>
